{
 "note": "the sails (docs/shipkit-5): each sail's objects, one per state (Set, Clewed, Furled: show one, hide the others) and a Head shown in every state (square sails and the spanker). parent: the spar the objects ride on (their origin and axes are its own: they hoist with it), or null (in the ship's frame). Set is full of wind with the yards square and the wind aft (square sails) and on the port tack (the others). The starboard tack is the Set mirrored about info's starboard_tack_mirror plane (point_m, normal; in the ship's frame, or the named frame's): the vertical plane through the sail's stay, which keeps its luff on the stay (the stays' feet are off the centreline), or the gaff's for the spanker. Clewed hangs from the yard hoisted; Furled lies on it lowered for a topsail, topgallant or royal (rig.json's hoist_m[0]: hoisted, its stay runs through the bunt) and where it is for a course. A square sail's clews belong at the yard below's sheaves (a course's at the ship's side): braced, the Set turned rigidly with its yard is only near (its clews part from the yard below by up to 28 in at 30 deg), so the game must draw the foot to the yard below. brace_deg: how far its yard braces with this sail set (rig.json's limit, or less where the set sail meets the rigging first, less 1 deg); ease_m [[deg, m]] (lower and topsail yards): how far forward its yard's truss or parrel lets it come as it braces with this sail set, used as rig.json's ease_m (the same or more: a sail's head, robands and earings stand a little off the yard). info: each sail's size and corners (metres, the ship's frame or, for *_local_m, the yard's; clew_cut_local_m is the clew as the sail is cut and the draught draws it)",
